// `args()` in the AOT backend (BACKLOG §6 item 25).
//
// The entry point builds an array from the `(argc, argv)` it receives and the
// chunk stores it in a hidden `$args` global, skipping `argv[0]` exactly like
// the VM. The harness passes the same vector to both runs (`-DOSKEL_ARGS`), so
// the values are compared by content rather than by shape -- including one
// argument with a space in it, which a naive tokeniser would split in two.
//
// Only the targets whose entry receives an argument vector can back this
// builtin: every hosted target (the Windows `main` wrapper moves the CRT's
// rcx/rdx, and the own linker's `_start` reads `__getmainargs`) and freestanding
// Linux. A freestanding Windows image and bare metal reject it by name, which
// is what `tests/native_build_args_error.oskl` pins.

var rest = args();
print("args type", type(rest));
print("args count", len(rest));
var i = 0;
for (a in rest) {
  print("arg", i, a);
  i = i + 1;
}
